[R-MO]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-03","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MO"},{"bioguideId":"C001035","fullName":"Sen. Collins, Susan M. [R-ME]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-04-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"ME"},{"bioguideId":"C001056","fullName":"Sen. Cornyn, John [R-TX]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-05-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T05:17:02+00:00","id":"s213-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-23","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-23","text":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Finance."},"laws":[],"number":"213","originChamber":"Senate","policyArea":"Taxation","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"D000618","district":null,"fullName":"Sen. Daines, Steve [R-MT]","party":"R","state":"MT"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-23","actionDesc":"Introduced in Senate","text":"<p><strong>Main Street Tax Certainty Act </strong></p><p>This bill makes permanent the qualified business income (QBI) tax deduction.</p><p>Under current law, individuals, estates, and trusts may deduct the lower of (1) 20% of QBI from a qualified business, qualified real estate investment trust dividends, and qualified publicly traded partnership income; or (2) 20% of taxable income less net capital gain. (Some limitations apply.)</p><p>However, under current law, the&nbsp;QBI tax deduction expires after December 31, 2025. </p>","updateDate":"2025-05-01T18:54:49Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Main Street Tax Certainty Act","type":"s","updateDate":"2025-05-15T11:03:16Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-05-15T11:03:16Z"}
